 {"version_id": "struct-30", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Strengthen the success gate against placeholder or non-patch outputs", "target_failure_mode": "Insufficient validation and iterative debugging", "expected_dimension": "execution_accuracy", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "evaluation/patch_selection/trae_selector/selector_agent.py", "find": "        self.is_success_patch = bool(is_success_patch and self.cleaned_patch and self.has_patch_content)", "replace": "        self.is_success_patch = bool(\n            is_success_patch\n            and self.has_patch_content\n            and not re.fullmatch(r\"(?is)(?:diff\\s+--git|---|\\+\\+\\+|no\\s+changes?)\\s*\", self.cleaned_patch)\n        )"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.86, "reasoning_soundness": 0.82, "execution_accuracy": 0.8, "output_integrity": 0.95}, "aggregate": 0.8575, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.22}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.18}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0225, "why": "The strengthened success gate blocks placeholder and non-patch text from being accepted, giving the best output-integrity improvement and a slight execution benefit by preventing false positives. It does not help solve the underlying hard repository tasks and may reject edge-case outputs that contain minimal but meaningful diff markers."}
 {"version_id": "prompt-01", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Repository reconnaissance and dependency tracing", "target_failure_mode": "Complex repository-specific diagnosis and implementation", "expected_dimension": "reasoning_soundness", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "For framework and scientific-library changes, build a behavior matrix before editing:", "replace": "Before editing a framework or scientific-library change, first perform repository reconnaissance: locate the primary implementation, all callers, related subclasses or alternate backends, existing regression tests, and analogous behavior elsewhere in the repository. Trace the relevant data and control flow, state the likely root cause, and identify the smallest compatible change. Then build a beha"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.9, "reasoning_soundness": 0.87, "execution_accuracy": 0.83, "output_integrity": 0.88}, "aggregate": 0.87, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.29}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.25}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.035, "why": "Repository reconnaissance directly addresses the diagnosed repository-specific failures by exposing callers, subclasses, and analogous implementations. It improves diagnosis and reduces missed integration points, but adds process overhead and does not itself ensure iterative validation, so execution gains are moderate rather than large."}
 {"version_id": "prompt-02", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Contract-first implementation planning", "target_failure_mode": "Complex repository-specific diagnosis and implementation", "expected_dimension": "reasoning_soundness", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "For framework and scientific-library changes, build a behavior matrix before editing:", "replace": "Before editing a framework or scientific-library change, convert the request into an explicit contract: list the current behavior, requested behavior, invariants that must remain unchanged, affected call sites, and compatibility constraints. Search for the implementation and its tests, compare nearby analogous APIs, and explain why the selected edit is the correct integration point. Then build a b"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.91, "reasoning_soundness": 0.88, "execution_accuracy": 0.82, "output_integrity": 0.88}, "aggregate": 0.8725, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.3}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.24}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "proposed_not_applied", "apply_note": "find-block matched 0x (need exactly 1)", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0375, "why": "An explicit behavioral contract improves requirement interpretation and compatibility reasoning, slightly exceeding reconnaissance for alignment. However, planning alone does not force complete repository tracing or test convergence, and overformalization can leave implementation defects unresolved."}
+{"version_id": "prompt-03", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Mandatory test-driven convergence loop", "target_failure_mode": "Insufficient validation and iterative debugging", "expected_dimension": "execution_accuracy", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "Before finalizing, perform an adversarial compatibility review covering", "replace": "After every nontrivial edit, run the narrowest relevant test or a focused reproduction, inspect the complete failure output, and iterate on the implementation until the focused checks pass. Then run the broader relevant test groups and, before finalizing, perform an adversarial compatibility review covering"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.88, "reasoning_soundness": 0.9, "execution_accuracy": 0.89, "output_integrity": 0.89}, "aggregate": 0.89, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.35}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.32}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.055, "why": "The mandatory focused-test and broader-test loop most directly repairs insufficient validation and iterative debugging, producing the strongest execution improvement. It still cannot compensate for an incorrect initial repository diagnosis, and mandatory testing can add cost or expose environment noise."}
+{"version_id": "prompt-04", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Failure-classification and escalation protocol", "target_failure_mode": "Insufficient validation and iterative debugging", "expected_dimension": "execution_accuracy", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "Before finalizing, perform an adversarial compatibility review covering", "replace": "When a test fails, classify it as an implementation defect, an unmet edge case, an incorrect test assumption, or an environment issue; inspect the traceback and relevant runtime values, make one focused correction at a time, and rerun the smallest reproducer before expanding test scope. Do not finalize while unexplained failures remain; before finalizing, perform an adversarial compatibility revie"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.85, "reasoning_soundness": 0.86, "execution_accuracy": 0.84, "output_integrity": 0.87}, "aggregate": 0.855, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.28}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.25}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "proposed_not_applied", "apply_note": "find-block matched 0x (need exactly 1)", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.02, "why": "Failure classification encourages disciplined debugging and prevents blindly changing code, but it is less powerful than a full convergence loop and risks incorrectly labeling a genuine defect as an environment or test issue. Gains are therefore small, with target alignment slightly below baseline due to added decision overhead."}
